  "slug": "best-of-bristol-2015-music",
  "title": "Best of Bristol 2015: Music",
  "content": "<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/the-fix-gigs-637x450.jpg\" alt=\"the-fix---gigs\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-10658\" height=\"450\" width=\"637\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/the-fix-gigs-637x450.jpg 637w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/the-fix-gigs-300x212.jpg 300w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/the-fix-gigs.jpg 842w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 637px) 100vw, 637px\" /></p>\n<p>As the year draws to a close, we&#8217;re looking at the best that Bristol has had to offer over the last twelve months. First up, we run down the best <strong>Music</strong> and pick the gig that we think has stood out above any others.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/villagers-6-e1450869827193-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Villagers, St George's\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-7303 size-thumbnail\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/villagers-6-e1450869827193-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/villagers-6-e1450869827193-45x45.jpg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A perfect marriage of band and venue, the always lovely indie folk of Dublin’s <b><a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/villagers-st-georges/\" target=\"_blank\">Villagers</a> </b>sounded suitably divine when set within ecclesiastical surroundings and wonderful acoustics of St. George&#8217;s. An exquisite night of music, frontman Conor O’Brien’s beautifully expressive vocals and additions of harp and flugelhorn saw delicate reworkings of old favourites and, with new album <i>Darling Arithmetic</i> just a day old, stunning versions from O’Brien’s stripped back “coming out” record.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/skILk-Kb5YKl7Wg43kLak2-3t59VJJRPiKKtt4Dhq8k9Fal_XEwboYopkUyt7ZCNawf-vgTcS6OYIWgdi-BqUc-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"skILk-Kb5YKl7Wg43kLak2-3t59VJJRPiKKtt4Dhq8k,9Fal_XEwboYopkUyt7ZCNawf-vgTcS6OYIWgdi-BqUc\" class=\"alignright size-thumbnail wp-image-10591\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/skILk-Kb5YKl7Wg43kLak2-3t59VJJRPiKKtt4Dhq8k9Fal_XEwboYopkUyt7ZCNawf-vgTcS6OYIWgdi-BqUc-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/skILk-Kb5YKl7Wg43kLak2-3t59VJJRPiKKtt4Dhq8k9Fal_XEwboYopkUyt7ZCNawf-vgTcS6OYIWgdi-BqUc-45x45.jpg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" />Taking us backwards and forwards through 50 years of music, British Invasion survivors <b><a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/the-zombies/\" target=\"_blank\">The Zombies</a></b> delivered a thrilling show within the intimacy of The Fleece. 70 year old singer Colin Blunstone’s age defying vocal abilities, Rod Argent’s keyboard wizardry and five successive cuts from the group’s 1968 masterpiece <i>Odessey &amp; Oracle,</i> were just a few of many factors that made this performance such fun. Enjoyed equally by people young and old, this was truly one of the warmest and most inclusive of gig-going experiences. <strong>(SH)</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/sunra-4-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Sun Ra Arkestra at The Lantern\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-6816 size-thumbnail\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/sunra-4-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/sunra-4-45x45.jpg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Aside from interviewing the awesome </span><b><a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/the-fix-podcast-matthew-e-white/\" target=\"_blank\">Matthew E. White</a> </b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">ahead of his gig at the Marble Factory, there were two standout music experiences for me in 2015. In March at The Lantern </span><b><a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/review-sun-ra-arkestra-the-lantern/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Ra Arkestra</a></b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> continued the pioneering legacy of Sun Ra, afrofuturist jazz pioneer and band leader. Under the distinctive guidance of nonagenarian saxophonist Marshall Allen, the band continue to be an incredible force, proving themselves to still be one of the most exuberant and inventive jazz outfits in the world. </span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/Goat-3-e1428476067313-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"REVIEW: Goat, Circomedia\" class=\"alignright wp-image-7131 size-thumbnail\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/Goat-3-e1428476067313-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/Goat-3-e1428476067313-45x45.jpg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In April, meanwhile, mysterious Swedish band </span><b><a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/review-goat-circomedia/\" target=\"_blank\">Goat</a></b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> entertained Circomedia as part of the Red Bull Music Academy weekend. Punters were instructed to leave their subjectivities &#8211; and mobile phones &#8211; at the door, and were supplied with shamanic kaftans and Eyes Wide Shut-style golden masks in order to create a mass of anonymous onlookers. It was a bold and engaging move from the band, who proceeded to crack out their danceable psych-rock under projections of nuclear explosions, brain scans and creepy little girls waving. <strong>(</strong><strong>CD)</strong></span></p>\n<p><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"GOAT - Gathering of Ancient Tribes, Live in Athens (17/Oct/2015, Gagarin 205)\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/rmzcn0WayeU?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></p>\n<hr />\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/ghostpoet-1-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"ghostpoet-1\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-7088 size-thumbnail\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/ghostpoet-1-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/ghostpoet-1-45x45.jpg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></p>\n<p>Many months before his second Mercury Music Prize nomination O<span>baro Ejimiwe, aka Coventry MC and rapper <strong><a href=\"http://baro%20Ejimiwe, aka Coventry MC and rapper Ghostpoet\" target=\"_blank\">Ghostpoet</a>,</strong> was flooring crowds with his now critically acclaimed album <em>Shedding Skin.</em></span> In an adoring and sweaty hot-box atmosphere at The Exchange the likes of ‘Meltdown’, ‘Sorry My Love, It’s You Not Me’, ‘Survive It’ and ‘Off Peak Dreams’ gave a hint to the uber-succesful year Poet was to enjoy.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/lauradoggett-2-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"REVIEW: Laura Doggett, Bristol Birdcage\" class=\"alignright wp-image-6744 size-thumbnail\" height=\"150\" width=\"150\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/lauradoggett-2-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/lauradoggett-2-45x45.jpg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" /></p>\n<p>The now sadly defunct Birdcage hosted a tantalisingly beautiful show by <strong><a href=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/review-laura-doggett-the-birdcage/\" target=\"_blank\">Laura Doggett</a></strong><em><strong> </strong></em><strong></strong>back in March. <span>Like Florence Welch in slow motion, Doggett has an adroitly serene and equally unique voice that fit like a glove in the respectful and relaxed surrounds of the old venue. And o</span><span>n that night she was in great form, despite her deprecating comments to the contrary. </span>Dressed like a Byzantium princess her performance was a celebration of the journey thus far and an emotional moment &#8211; at times being visibly overwhelmed at being back “home”. <strong>(KM)</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/And-the-winner-is-red-300x263.png\" alt=\"And the winner is red\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-10752\" height=\"263\" width=\"300\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/And-the-winner-is-red-300x263.png 300w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/And-the-winner-is-red-768x673.png 768w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/And-the-winner-is-red-514x450.png 514w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/And-the-winner-is-red.png 1972w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/GOAT_08-AC-730x450.png\" alt=\"GOAT_08-AC\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-10795 size-large\" height=\"450\" width=\"730\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/GOAT_08-AC-730x450.png 730w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/GOAT_08-AC-300x185.png 300w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/GOAT_08-AC-768x474.png 768w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/GOAT_08-AC.png 798w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 730px) 100vw, 730px\" /></p>\n<p>Not only a delight to the ears, this was also a visual feast too &#8211; a tribal experience without peers.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Contributions by Kevin McGough (KM), Conal Dougan (CD) and Scott Hammond (SH).</strong></p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"></p>",
